Given the following Python code, match each property accessed on `rect` with the value it produces. The properties are accessed without parentheses because `@property` exposes each computed method like an attribute.

```python
class Rectangle:
    def __init__(self, width, height):
        self._width = width
        self._height = height

    @property
    def area(self):
        return self._width * self._height

    @property
    def perimeter(self):
        return 2 * (self._width + self._height)

    @property
    def is_square(self):
        return self._width == self._height

    @property
    def description(self):
        return f"{self._width}x{self._height}"

rect = Rectangle(4, 6)
```

